# SNIP architecture (this repository)

This repo is the first **SNIP domain application** (Network Planning & Optimisation), not the entire Simba Network Intelligence Platform.

Read before changing code:

- `docs/implementation/SNIP-IMPLEMENTATION-CONTEXT.md` (section 0 is authoritative for scope)
- `docs/implementation/SNIP-IMPLEMENTATION-STATUS.md`
- `docs/architecture/NIP-PHASE-4-GOVERNED-ACTION-MCP-ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `docs/implementation/SNIP-PHASE-4-GOVERNED-ACTION-MCP-SPECIFICATION.md`

Root copies also exist:

- `NIP-PHASE-4-GOVERNED-ACTION-MCP-ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `SNIP-PHASE-4-GOVERNED-ACTION-MCP-SPECIFICATION.md`

## Authorised now

Phase **4** is architecturally accepted and **frozen** on the Phase 3 baseline (`c692eb8d42711ed523460d2de34ffb0a607e7f17`). Do not add Phase 4 functionality, resolve deferred technical debt, or refactor for its own sake.

Preserve Phase 1A/1A.1/1B/2/3/4. Kafka remains off by default. Do not vectorize operational telemetry or Assurance Case state. Detection remains deterministic. The LLM explains and prioritises investigation; it does not decide thresholds, severity, confidence, risk, or policy. AI may propose. Deterministic policy decides. Humans approve where required. MCP invokes only registered capabilities.

Same-JVM loopback JSON-RPC HTTP MCP is accepted. The in-code capability registry is accepted. Phase 4 POST APIs mutate SNIP governance state only and do not authorise live network mutation. Failed-result row replacement remains deferred technical debt.

Governance POST APIs mutate SNIP workflow state only. They must never write to the live network. Direct LLM-to-MCP invocation is prohibited.

## Do not implement

Autonomous agents, Agent Factory, live OSS/NMS/EMS integrations, live gNB/network writes, Ericsson ENM / Nokia NetAct writes, auto-remediation, incident-management / ITSM, Schema Registry, Avro, Protobuf, Flink, Spark, Kafka Streams, dedicated time-series DB, EKS/Kubernetes, Kong, ALB, ALICE, RL, ML anomaly detection, adaptive thresholds, forecasting, billing, Ionic, AWS lock-in, production IAM/OIDC, remote third-party MCP, vendor MCP adapters, production RF simulation, full Digital Twin execution, network rollback, Phase 5.

## Rules

- Extend Phase 1A/1B/2/3 abstractions. Do not rewrite the slice.
- Keep recommendation and domain APIs read-only for the network. Action execute/approve mutate SNIP governance state only.
- If retrieval is empty, do not fabricate citations.
- Ordinary CI must not download large models. PostgreSQL via Testcontainers remains required. Kafka Testcontainers remains allowed.
- Implementation markdown lives under `docs/implementation/`. ADRs under `docs/architecture/adr/`.
- Architecture document has architectural authority. Implementation specification is the authorised execution scope.
- Do not push or establish a new Git baseline until the Phase 4 completion report has been reviewed and explicit architectural acceptance has been granted.
